          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A breaker finder is only as good as the two steps around it: calibrating on the panel so one breaker stands out, and switching that breaker off to prove the answer. With those, a budget finder is accurate enough to map a whole house; without them, an expensive one will mislead you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Treat every reading as a hypothesis, confirm it at the outlet, verify dead with a tester before you touch wiring, and label as you go. If you are choosing a tool, our <a href="/best-circuit-breaker-finder/">tested breaker finder picks</a> cover which ones cope best with crowded and AFCI-heavy panels.
